  "narrative": "These are discovery evidence assessments in the supplied dataset only. For the direction -1 claims tested here, a positive signed mean difference means the exposed group has more negative dependency_composite values, i.e. stronger composite dependency. A positive signed interaction means the exposed-minus-comparator stronger-dependency association is augmented in the named context relative to its complement.\n\nThe main CDKN2A_loss follow-up remains borderline rather than decisive. H139 estimates the stronger-dependency CDKN2A association within TP53-wildtype/KEAP1-wildtype cells at +0.144 [0.075, 0.213]. It is statistically nonzero and close to the 0.15 threshold, but its point estimate is below the threshold and its interval includes both subthreshold and threshold-exceeding effects. I therefore leave H139 unresolved and active. H140 in TP53-loss/KEAP1-wildtype cells is too imprecise for a meaningful effect-size claim: +0.135 [0.005, 0.265], with the point estimate below threshold and the interval very wide because the exposed cell is small. I leave it unresolved but deferred rather than active. H141 in TP53-wildtype/KEAP1-loss cells is near null, +0.034 [-0.107, 0.175], so the stronger-dependency claim is rejected. The lineage checks are mixed: adenocarcinoma, H142, is just above threshold at +0.153 [0.067, 0.239], but the lower bound is far below threshold, so I keep it unresolved active; squamous, H143, is +0.103 [-0.045, 0.250], not statistically meaningful and below threshold, so it is rejected. The high-screen-quality stratum H144 gives +0.116 [0.014, 0.219]: the association is statistically nonzero but the point estimate is below the meaningfulness threshold and the interval crosses it, so it remains unresolved active. Direct CDKN2A interactions do not support meaningful positive modification: H145 by TP53_loss is +0.063 [-0.098, 0.224], and H146 by KEAP1_loss is -0.037 [-0.206, 0.131]. Both intervals include zero and do not establish reliable augmentation of the stronger-dependency association, so both are rejected. The interval for H146 does have a negative side that could suggest attenuation, but because it crosses zero, there is not reliable evidence for a meaningful opposite interaction; I reject the registered positive interaction without claiming attenuation.\n\nThe clearest new main-effect discovery is PTEN_loss. H147 estimates a stronger-dependency association of +0.239 units [0.145, 0.332]. The point estimate is substantially above the 0.15 threshold and the interval excludes zero and a broad range of subthreshold effects. The lower bound is very slightly below 0.15, but the effect estimate is much larger than CDKN2A and the uncertainty is not dominated by null-like or widely imprecise values. I therefore accept H147 as a dataset-specific observational association while keeping investigation active and requesting independent validation of H147. This should not be interpreted as causality or generalizability; it is a candidate association in this supplied dataset that merits replication and biological interpretation later. I also reassessed the opposite-direction PTEN claim H38. Its evidence R61 is signed to the weaker-dependency hypothesis and is negative, -0.239 [-0.332, -0.145], meaning PTEN_loss is associated with stronger rather than weaker dependency in the raw contrast. H38 is rejected and closed.\n\nThe remaining broad tests did not reveal new meaningful main effects. NF1_loss H148 is -0.014 [-0.112, 0.083], BRCA2_loss H149 is +0.029 [-0.091, 0.148], and APC_mutation H150 is -0.001 [-0.083, 0.082]. All are far below the threshold and statistically compatible with no meaningful effect in the stronger-dependency direction, so each is rejected and closed. For consistency, I also reassessed the opposite-direction claims H42, H41, and H70 using the same evidence: H42 NF1 weaker is null, H41 BRCA2 weaker is null/opposite, and H70 APC weaker is null; all are rejected and closed.\n\nOverall, the currently strongest dataset-specific observational findings remain TP53_loss and KEAP1_loss associated with weaker dependency and SMARCA4_loss associated with stronger dependency. PTEN_loss is now a promising new stronger-dependency candidate and is the target for independent validation. CDKN2A_loss remains borderline: the main effect and several strata are near threshold but do not clearly exceed it. I registered follow-up PTEN robustness/conditional and interaction proposals, plus a CDKN2A-by-lineage interaction, to make better use of later iterations.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration-5 appraise. Direction -1: positive mean difference = stronger dependency; positive interaction = augmentation of stronger-dependency association. CDKN2A remains borderline: H112 main unresolved; H139 TP53wt/KEAP1wt +0.144 [0.075,0.213] unresolved; H142 adenocarcinoma +0.153 [0.067,0.239] unresolved; H144 high ROC +0.116 [0.014,0.219] unresolved; H140 small and imprecise unresolved deferred; H141, H143, H145, H146 rejected/closed. No decisive CDKN2A conditional exceeds threshold with lower bound above 0.15.\n\nNew main candidate: PTEN_loss H147 accepted active as dataset-specific stronger-dependency association: +0.239 [0.145,0.332], lower just below threshold but point large. Independent validation requested for H147. Reassess H147 when validation response appears; if validation evidence is inconsistent or threshold-clear, update. H38 opposite weaker PTEN rejected/closed on R61.\n\nOther broad tests negative: NF1 H148, BRCA2 H149, APC H150 rejected. Reassessed opposite claims H42/H41/H70 rejected/closed. Next priorities: PTEN conditional/interaction robustness and CDKN2A-by-lineage interaction registered; keep all claims observational and non-causal.",
